{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 3, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n5le01ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n5le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob08re2img01.jpg", "text": "<strong>Sam</strong>: Hey, Lucy! How are you?<br/>\n<strong>Lucy</strong>: Hi, Sam! I'm fine, but I'm really worried about the final test.<br/>\n<strong>Sam</strong>: I know. I feel the same. We'd better study together so that we feel more confident.<br/>\n<strong>Lucy</strong>: You're right, Sam. You know what? I have serious problems with security in the .NET Framework.<br/>\n<strong>Sam</strong>: Well, It's not difficult. It simply improves the security in your computer with something called Code Access Security.<br/>\n<strong>Lucy</strong>: That's exactly what's unclear to me. What is it?<br/>", "time": "0"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob08re2img02.jpg", "text": "<strong>Sam</strong>: It's an infrastructure that allows people to differentiate permissions or rights that a code has from the rights that you have. Remember that, in the past, every code on a computer had the same rights to access resources as you did as a user of the computer. It means there were no restrictions to access the information of the computer.<br/>\n<strong>Lucy</strong>: I see. What are the characteristics of Code Access security?<br/>\n<strong>Sam</strong>: It protects computer systems from malicious code and protects trusted code from accidentally compromising security; additionally, it gives you more control over the applications you want to perform by limiting the action of those on your computer. Program users might want to work in a virus-controlled environment.  <br/>", "time": "31000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob08re2img03.jpg", "text": "<strong>Lucy</strong>: So, this affects the development of applications, right?<br/>\n<strong>Sam</strong>: Sure. The first thing you ought to guarantee when developing an application is security. Then, you have to decide how the application will perform in a semi-trusted or less than a full-trust environment. These environments will need a different application design. The safest applications are created considering the permissions you grant as a programmer.<br/>\n<strong>Lucy</strong>: Thanks, Sam! Now everything is clear to me. I hope I do well in the test.", "time": "73000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about the role of code access security infrastructure in the .NET framework.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can present features of code access security in the .NET framework.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can discuss information about developing an application in the .NET framework.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Is your computer safe from any virus? Why? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What measures have to be taken to keep our programs secure?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "We had better keep our programs safe.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "STI", "stimuli_ids": [3], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"id": 0, "responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 