l <b>had better use</b> the .NET framework.</li> <li>Jessica <strong>ought to</strong> write a letter to ask for a change in the program.</li> <li>You <strong>might want to</strong> ask for help if you have doubts using the program.</li></span> </ul> The structure of these forms are always the same regardless the subject.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We'd better study together so that we feel more confident.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The first thing you ought to guarantee when developing an application is security. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Degrees of Trust Granted on an Application", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There is a difference between the code that runs on your computer and the code that is created to run on other machines.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The degree of trust granted on an application depends on where the code resides and how it is started. When creating an application, it is important to be aware of the degrees of trust that are granted by default in each computer:<br/><br/><ol><li><strong>Full trust permission set</strong>: This is the code that the local computer grants.</li><li><strong>Local intranet permission set</strong>: It is granted by the local network.</li><li><strong>Internet permission set</strong>: This code is granted by the internet.</li></ol>These default values may affect the permissions to your application. This means that the application can work differently on each computer depending on the security policy; for instance, if your application requires an internet connection to update, the program will not update unless you have access to the internet. Otherwise, the user has to change the security settings to allow it.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "trust ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "reliance on the security of something  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Then, you have to decide how the application will perform in a semi-trusted or less than a full-trust environment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "malicious code ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a kind of harmful computer code that makes the system vulnerable to damage or data theft ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It protects computer systems from malicious code and protects trusted code from accidentally compromising security.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "code", "type": "name"}, {"content": "symbolic representation of statements or instructions in a computer program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: It's an infrastructure that allows people to differentiate permissions or rights that a code has from the rights that you have.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "compromise ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to expose in danger ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It protects computer systems from malicious code and protects trusted code from accidentally compromising security.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "application", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a program intended to perform a specific function directly for a user", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The first thing you ought to guarantee when developing an application is security.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "grant ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give or confer  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The safest applications are created considering the permissions you grant as a programmer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n5le01ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write why Code Access Security is important. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Check with your teacher the information that you wrote. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the information with your classmates.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about Code Access Security ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the information about Code Access Security with my teacher", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about Code Access Security with my classmates", "type": "text"}]}]}